{"id":"leetcode-779","version":1,"status":"approved","title":"K-th Symbol in Grammar","summary":"Construct a table with n rows, starting with 0 in the first row.","statement":"Construct a table with n rows, starting with 0 in the first row. Each subsequent row replaces 0 with 01 and 1 with 10. Given n and k, find the k-th (1-indexed) symbol in the n-th row.","constraints":["1 <= n <= 30 and 1 <= k <= 2^(n-1).","Each zero expands to 01 and each one to 10; return the one-indexed kth symbol."],"topics":["recursion","bit-manipulation"],"prerequisites":[],"signature":{"name":"kth_grammar_symbol","parameters":[{"name":"n","annotation":"int","adapter":"raw","source_parameter":null},{"name":"k","annotation":"int","adapter":"raw","source_parameter":null}],"returns":"int","return_adapter":"raw","node_policy":"values","result_mode":"return","mutated_parameter":null,"immutable_parameters":[]},"starter_code":"def kth_grammar_symbol(n: int, k: int) -> int:\n    # Write your solution here.\n    pass\n","reference_solution":"def kth_grammar_symbol(n, k):\n    return (k-1).bit_count()%2\n","brute_force_solution":null,"known_wrong_solutions":["def kth_grammar_symbol(n, k):\n    return (k).bit_count()%2\n","def kth_grammar_symbol(n,k):\n    return (k-1)%2\n"],"target_time_complexity":"O(log k)","target_space_complexity":"O(1)","estimated_minutes":35,"rubric":{"algorithmic_insight":2,"prerequisites":1,"implementation":1,"performance_pressure":1,"edge_cases":0},"hints":["A position flips once for every one bit in its zero-based index.","Use parity of popcount(k-1), equivalent to recursive parent tracing.","Return bit_count(k-1) modulo two.","Every right-child choice flips the parent symbol; those choices are exactly the one bits of k-1."],"editorial":"Every right-child choice flips the parent symbol; those choices are exactly the one bits of k-1.","tests":[{"id":"lc-779-1","arguments":[1,1],"expected":0,"comparator":"exact","visible":true,"explanation":"The first row contains only zero.